# The trial of pod-oci in podvm (T-056), at podvm main cb57d4b (commit).
# The trial builds against the crates of the tag of the hand-off
# (pod-oci.tag), as podvm takes them.
# The patch applies alone. After the patches of pod-guest and pod-enter of
# v0.9.0 (podvm took them at 423e817), with git apply --3way, only the tag
# lines (take v0.10.0), the pod-* rows of docs/runtime-state.md (keep each
# row, at 0.10.0) and two adjacent citation lines of T-1684 in TODO/gate.md
# (keep both) conflict.
# crates/podvm-image keeps the store, the pull into it, save, load and
# import, net.rs, AcceptAny, docker's codes and podvm's glue:
# registry::client (podvm's transport, trust, AcceptAny for an insecure
# registry, the logins of credentials::files(), a move to plain HTTP as a
# line `podvm: ...` on stderr, the file-size ceiling), transport::resolve
# (the flags, PODVM_INSECURE_REGISTRIES, PODVM_CONFIG and its file),
# platform::wanted (PODVM_DEFAULT_PLATFORM, DOCKER_DEFAULT_PLATFORM),
# credentials::{lookup, store_login, remove_login, default_paths} at $HOME
# and $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, tls::{client_config, host_bundle_bytes} over
# pod_oci::trust, the Store as pod_oci::pull::Blobs, and
# Error::Image(pod_core::Failure) with From<Failure> (NoPlatform and
# DigestMismatch keep their variants; Class::Usage is docker's 1). reference,
# digest and oci are pod_oci's modules; 7 files leave podvm. Each podcrates
# tag moves to v0.10.0, with the tags of podvm-supervise. The
# disclosure of the policy gets podvm's prefix. The call sites of
# Platform::wanted and Policy::resolve call podvm's functions; the
# citations of the moved files name pod-oci. podvm's tests of the touched
# crates (with the fixture pulls of podvm-image) and the integration tests
# of the command line; clippy of the workspace and rustfmt of the touched
# crates; the runtime-state rows; podvm's record gate; each Rust toolchain
# of the workflows against the rust-version of podcrates; and the binary
# `podvm` for x86_64 musl, with podcrates' static check.
# podvm's binary embeds its interposer objects (crates/podvm/build.rs), and
# the tests of qol need them on a host that denies chroot(2), as a runner
# does. podvm's gate.yml builds them before the binary; the trial does the
# same.
cargo build -q --release -p podvm-gate --bin podvm-interpose-build
mkdir -p target/release && cp "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/podvm-interpose-build" target/release/
./target/release/podvm-interpose-build
cargo test -q -p podvm-image
cargo test -q -p podvm-extract
cargo test -q -p podvm-complete
cargo test -q -p podvm-supervise
cargo test -q -p podvm --bin podvm
cargo test -q -p podvm --test store_gates
cargo test -q -p podvm --test qol
cargo test -q -p podvm --test curated_refusals
cargo clippy -q --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo fmt -p podvm-image -p podvm-extract -p podvm -p podvm-gate -p podvm-release --check
cargo build -q -p podvm --bin podvm
# podvm's gate finds the root of the repository from the path of its binary,
# so it runs from target/release/, with document-state beside it (gate.yml).
cargo build -q --release -p podvm-gate && cargo build -q --release -p podvm-release --bin document-state
mkdir -p target/release && cp "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/podvm-gate" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/document-state" target/release/
# docs/runtime-state.md lists each direct git or registry dependency with its
# locked version. The patch gives the rows of the git form (pod-core,
# pod-hostprobe, pod-oci, pod-proxy, pod-supervise, pod-term and pod-tls at
# 0.10.0); the
# trial's path form has no row for them. Each other row of the patch must be
# the generated one.
grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md > target/runtime-state.patch.md && python3 scripts/document-state.py --write && grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md | diff target/runtime-state.patch.md -
./target/release/podvm-gate
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
sh "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-static.sh" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podvm"
